1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,368
Why does Iceland have no mosquitoes?

2
00:00:02,718 --> 00:00:06,160
Mosquitoes live almost everywhere on Earth, from

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:09,316
the tropics to the Arctic. Greenland, Norway

4
00:00:09,316 --> 00:00:12,830
and Scotland, Iceland's neighbors, all have them.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,420
But for a very long time, Iceland

6
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:17,252
had none. It was one of the

7
00:00:17,252 --> 00:00:20,510
only places, besides Antarctica, where you could

8
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:23,224
spend a summer evening outside without a

9
00:00:23,224 --> 00:00:24,039
single bite.

10
00:00:24,389 --> 00:00:27,672
Scientists aren't completely sure why. The most

11
00:00:27,672 --> 00:00:30,745
popular idea is the weather. Mosquitoes need

12
00:00:30,745 --> 00:00:33,050
still water to lay eggs and grow.

13
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,448
Iceland's winters often freeze and thaw again

14
00:00:36,448 --> 00:00:39,089
and again. A mosquito larva might hatch

15
00:00:39,089 --> 00:00:41,527
during a warm spell, then get frozen

16
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:43,491
before it can finish growing.

17
00:00:43,841 --> 00:00:46,725
Iceland does have other bugs, though. Lake

18
00:00:46,725 --> 00:00:50,089
Mývatn literally means midge lake, because clouds

19
00:00:50,089 --> 00:00:52,630
of tiny midges swarm there in summer.

20
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:56,210
Then, in October 2025, came the surprise.

21
00:00:56,210 --> 00:00:59,518
An insect lover near Reykjavík found three

22
00:00:59,518 --> 00:01:02,747
mosquitoes, believed to be the first ever

23
00:01:02,747 --> 00:01:05,268
recorded in the wild in Iceland.

24
00:01:05,618 --> 00:01:08,561
They were a cold-tolerant species that can

25
00:01:08,561 --> 00:01:11,855
survive winter as adults. Scientists say warmer

26
00:01:11,855 --> 00:01:14,448
weather and more ships and planes may

27
00:01:14,448 --> 00:01:17,181
help insects like this arrive and stay.

28
00:01:17,531 --> 00:01:20,924
Antarctica is the other big mosquito-free place.

29
00:01:20,924 --> 00:01:23,186
It's simply too cold and dry for

30
00:01:23,186 --> 00:01:26,225
them, though one tiny flightless midge does

31
00:01:26,225 --> 00:01:27,003
live there.

32
00:01:27,353 --> 00:01:30,632
Iceland's neighbors aren't so lucky. In Greenland

33
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:33,711
and northern Scandinavia, summer swarms can be

34
00:01:33,711 --> 00:01:36,121
so thick that hikers wear head nets.

35
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:39,362
Iceland is also very strict about bringing

36
00:01:39,362 --> 00:01:41,909
in animals and plants, partly to keep

37
00:01:41,909 --> 00:01:44,181
new pests and diseases out of the

38
00:01:44,181 --> 00:01:44,663
island.

39
00:01:45,013 --> 00:01:47,986
So, is Iceland's mosquito-free era over? Would

40
00:01:47,986 --> 00:01:50,184
you still visit if it wasn't? Tell

41
00:01:50,184 --> 00:01:51,413
me in the comments.

